# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Your own answers and reports
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# An answers file describes your organization's weak spots -- treat it as
# internal material. The bundled `answers.example.*` files are the only ones
# that belong in the repository (see SECURITY.md).
*answers*.csv
*answers*.json
!scoring/answers.example.csv
!scoring/answers.example.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Generated test artifacts
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# `python3 test/run_tests.py` writes machine-specific output here (hostname
# Python version, timestamps). Regenerate it locally; never commit it.
test/results/

